Cognitive Field Computing recasts intelligence not as a property of isolated agents, but as a continuous medium—a literal field that permeates space and time, sustained by the physical infrastructure of computation and energy. In this view, the historical progression from mainframes to personal computers to the cloud is a gradual realization that computation, like electricity, is an infrastructure layer. The next step is to make cognition itself such a layer: always on, everywhere present, and as dependable as the laws of thermodynamics upon which it is built.

